### Player ratings & reliability - example requests (IntelliJ / VS Code REST Client)
### Replace the ids with real user ids from GET http://localhost:4000/users

@base = http://localhost:4000
@playerA = f9099e92-ce36-40dc-a69c-44960ba083f3
@playerB = efb574cf-4ceb-4289-a1cc-b1f28e25e7fd

### Player B rates player A after game g-101
POST {{base}}/users/{{playerA}}/ratings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "raterId": "{{playerB}}",
  "gameId": "g-101",
  "sport": "BADMINTON",
  "skill": 4,
  "sportsmanship": 5,
  "comment": "Great rallies, very fair on line calls"
}

### Ratings player A has received
GET {{base}}/users/{{playerA}}/ratings

### Match result: A beat B in singles -> updates both Elo ratings
POST {{base}}/matches/results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "gameId": "g-101",
  "sport": "BADMINTON",
  "winnerIds": ["{{playerA}}"],
  "loserIds": ["{{playerB}}"]
}

### Player B didn't turn up to game g-102
POST {{base}}/users/{{playerB}}/attendance
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "gameId": "g-102",
  "status": "NO_SHOW",
  "sport": "BADMINTON",
  "gameTime": "2026-10-14T18:00:00Z"
}

### Player B's reliability score and history
GET {{base}}/users/{{playerB}}/reliability

### Full player profile: Elo + peer ratings per sport + reliability
GET {{base}}/users/{{playerA}}/profile
